    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "My apologies for the confusion. An escrow agent, also known as an escrow officer, is a neutral third party who facilitates the transaction between buyer and seller. They hold onto the earnest money deposit as a form of security to ensure that both parties fulfill their contractual obligations. The agent's role is to verify that the buyer has the funds and that the seller has the property, then release the funds to the seller once all conditions of the sale are met. This process provides legal protection for both parties, ensuring that the buyer's deposit is returned if the sale doesn't go through, or is used to cover any agreed-upon expenses if the sale does proceed. The escrow agent acts as a safeguard against fraud and helps to ensure a smooth and fair transaction.",
